[34/158] rejected; issues=["The corrected rationale does not directly state a numeric final score, but it strongly implies a particular rubric level ('prevents it from meeting the highest standard'), which effectively leaks the band. It should describe the grounding and specificity issues without pointing toward a specific tier of the rubric.", "The final sentence frames the assessment as a rubric-level judgment ('prevents it from meeting the highest standard of explicit grounding combined with specificity'), which constitutes rubric application language. The rationale should critique the comment's qualities rather than adjudicate rubric placement.", "Original sentence 4's correction replaces the wrong score claim but still effectively conveys the same rubric verdict indirectly. It should simply state the deficiencies (vague reference, incomplete suggestion, lack of specificity) without referencing rubric tiers or 'highest standard.'"]
